From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Put the W541's USB connectors on their
 sides

The _PLD of the four USB connectors come from the OEM tables, which the
T440p and the W541 share. Plugging a USB 3.0 drive into each connector
of a W541 with PORTSC watched puts three of them on another panel than
those buffers say, and the Always On connector on another port: port 1
(HS01/SS01) is the connector on the left side farthest from the screen,
marked SS, not on the right; port 2 (HS02/SS02) is the connector on the
right side farthest from the screen, marked SS, not on the left; port 3
(HS03) is the connector on the left side nearest the screen, the Always
On one, not on the back; port 6 (HS06) is the connector on the right
side nearest the screen, as said. The OS shows the position to the
user only (Windows's port names, Linux's physical_location), so nothing
else changes.

Give the W541 buffers with the measured panels: left for ports 1 and 3,
right for ports 2 and 6, one row on each side, the horizontal position
telling the two apart as seen facing that side (the screen is on the
left when facing the left side, on the right when facing the right
one). The shape is a USB-A connector's, the group positions and the
rest of the bytes stay the OEM's. The T440p keeps the OEM buffers until
someone measures it.

TEST=iasl -tc -w3: the buffers compile and disassemble to LEFT/CENTER/
RIGHT (port 1), RIGHT/CENTER/LEFT (port 2), LEFT/CENTER/LEFT (port 3)
and RIGHT/CENTER/RIGHT (port 6) on the W541, the OEM values on the
T440p.
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl | 50 +++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl
index 1531df4b72..4977255c20 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
  * 2 left, 3 right, 4 front, 5 back) and VerticalPosition (6-7); byte 9 has
  * HorizontalPosition (bits 0-1) and Shape (2-5).
  *
- *  xHCI port  USB 3.0  OEM     connector
+ *  xHCI port  USB 3.0  OEM     connector, as the OEM tables say
  *  1          16       UPC0    USB 3.0, right (the Always On one)
  *  2          17       UPC1    USB 3.0, left
  *  3          -        UPC2    USB 2.0, back
@@ -25,6 +25,16 @@
  *  12         -        -       inside: the camera
  *  4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 14, 15, USB 3.0 18, 19, 21: nothing
  *
+ * On the W541 the four connectors are not where those buffers put them,
+ * measured by plugging a drive into each with PORTSC watched: port 1 is
+ * the connector on the left side farthest from the screen, the one marked
+ * SS; port 2 is the connector on the right side farthest from the screen,
+ * also marked SS; port 3 is the connector on the left side nearest the
+ * screen, the Always On one (not port 1 as the OEM tables say); port 6 is
+ * the connector on the right side nearest the screen. The W541 gets
+ * buffers with those panels and positions, the T440p keeps the OEM ones
+ * until someone measures it.
+ *
  * The OEM firmware marks the ports of the devices inside as not
  * connectable (what _UPC means by "nothing can ever be plugged there");
  * here they are connectable, with the OEM connector type, and not visible:
@@ -56,12 +66,38 @@
 #define PLD_EXPRESSCARD	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x48, 0x1D, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0, 0, 0
 #define PLD_INSIDE	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x30, 0x1C, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0, 0, 0
 
-USB_PORT(HS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_RIGHT)
-USB_PORT(HS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_LEFT)
-USB_PORT(HS03, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_USB2_BACK)
+#if CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541)
+/*
+ * The W541's connectors where they are, two on each side, one row. Byte 8:
+ * visible, the panel, the vertical position (center); byte 9: the
+ * horizontal position as seen facing that side (the screen is on the left
+ * when facing the left side, on the right when facing the right one), and
+ * the shape of a USB-A connector (4, a horizontal rectangle); bytes 10-11
+ * the OEM group positions of the two USB 3.0 ports; byte 12 as in the OEM
+ * buffers.
+ */
+/* Port 1: left side, farthest from the screen (SS) */
+#define PLD_PORT1	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x51, 0x12, 0x80, 0x00, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+/* Port 2: right side, farthest from the screen (SS) */
+#define PLD_PORT2	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x59, 0x10, 0x00, 0x01, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+/* Port 3: left side, nearest the screen, the Always On one */
+#define PLD_PORT3	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x51, 0x10, 0x00, 0x00, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+/* Port 6: right side, nearest the screen */
+#define PLD_PORT6	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x59, 0x12, 0x00, 0x00, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+#else
+/* The T440p: the OEM buffers, until someone measures its connectors */
+#define PLD_PORT1	PLD_USB3_RIGHT
+#define PLD_PORT2	PLD_USB3_LEFT
+#define PLD_PORT3	PLD_USB2_BACK
+#define PLD_PORT6	PLD_USB2_RIGHT
+#endif
+
+USB_PORT(HS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT1)
+USB_PORT(HS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT2)
+USB_PORT(HS03, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_PORT3)
 USB_PORT(HS04, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS05, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
-USB_PORT(HS06, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_USB2_RIGHT)
+USB_PORT(HS06, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_PORT6)
 USB_PORT(HS07, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS08, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS09, USB_YES, USB_OEM, PLD_DOCK)
@@ -71,8 +107,8 @@ USB_PORT(HS12, USB_YES, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS13, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS14, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS15, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
-USB_PORT(SS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_RIGHT)
-USB_PORT(SS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_LEFT)
+USB_PORT(SS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT1)
+USB_PORT(SS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT2)
 USB_PORT(SS03, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(SS04, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(SS05, USB_YES, USB_OEM, PLD_DOCK)
-- 
2.43.0

